{"id":"342ec644d0a0b06c8419cf153bf6963e8529641a","url":"https://github.com/vangelov/ts-rasterizer","title":"GitHub - vangelov/ts-rasterizer: A TypeScript software rasterizer with programmable shaders","site_name":"Buzzing","source":"github.com","byline":null,"excerpt":"A TypeScript software rasterizer with programmable shaders - vangelov/ts-rasterizer","content_html":"<DIV class=\"page\" id=\"readability-page-1\"><div data-hpc=\"true\" containertiming=\"hpc\"><article itemprop=\"text\"><P dir=\"auto\"><h2 dir=\"auto\" tabindex=\"-1\">Overview</h2><a id=\"user-content-overview\" aria-label=\"Permalink: Overview\" href=\"#overview\"></a></P>\n<p dir=\"auto\">A TypeScript CPU software rasterizer with programmable vertex and fragment shaders. Vertex layouts are fully customizable, allowing shaders to define and interpolate arbitrary vertex attributes.</p>\n<P dir=\"auto\"><h2 dir=\"auto\" tabindex=\"-1\">Credits</h2><a id=\"user-content-credits\" aria-label=\"Permalink: Credits\" href=\"#credits\"></a></P>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The renderer is heavily based on Nikolaus Rauch's excellent <a href=\"https://github.com/nikolausrauch/software-rasterizer\">C++ software rasterizer</a>. Everything else—including the vector and matrix library, texture handling, sampling, and browser integration—was implemented specifically for this project and designed around the constraints of TypeScript and the web. The demos are adapted from Nikolaus's original project.</p>\n<P dir=\"auto\"><h2 dir=\"auto\" tabindex=\"-1\">Demos</h2><a id=\"user-content-demos\" aria-label=\"Permalink: Demos\" href=\"#demos\"></a></P>\n<div dir=\"auto\">\n  <markdown-accessiblity-table><table>\n    <tbody><tr>\n      <td>\n        <a href=\"https://vangelov.github.io/ts-rasterizer/00-triangle.html\" rel=\"nofollow\">\n          <strong>Triangle</strong>\n        </a>\n      </td>\n      <td>\n        <a href=\"https://vangelov.github.io/ts-rasterizer/01-plane.html\" rel=\"nofollow\">\n          <strong>Plane</strong>\n        </a>\n      </td>\n      <td>\n        <a href=\"https://vangelov.github.io/ts-rasterizer/02-depth-buffer.html\" rel=\"nofollow\">\n          <strong>Depth</strong>\n        </a>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <a href=\"https://vangelov.github.io/ts-rasterizer/00-triangle.html\" rel=\"nofollow\">\n          <img src=\"/vangelov/ts-rasterizer/raw/main/screenshots/00-triangle.png\" width=\"250\" alt=\"Triangle\">\n        </a>\n      </td>\n      <td>\n        <a href=\"https://vangelov.github.io/ts-rasterizer/01-indexed-plane.html\" rel=\"nofollow\">\n          <img src=\"/vangelov/ts-rasterizer/raw/main/screenshots/01-indexed-plane.png\" width=\"250\" alt=\"Plane\">\n        </a>\n      </td>\n      <td>\n        <a href=\"https://vangelov.github.io/ts-rasterizer/02-depth-buffer.html\" rel=\"nofollow\">\n          <img src=\"/vangelov/ts-rasterizer/raw/main/screenshots/02-depth-buffer.png\" width=\"250\" alt=\"Depth\">\n        </a>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <a href=\"https://vangelov.github.io/ts-rasterizer/03-texture.html\" rel=\"nofollow\">\n          <strong>Texture</strong>\n        </a>\n      </td>\n      <td>\n        <a href=\"https://vangelov.github.io/ts-rasterizer/04-framebuffer.html\" rel=\"nofollow\">\n          <strong>Framebuffer</strong>\n        </a>\n      </td>\n      <td>\n        <a href=\"https://vangelov.github.io/ts-rasterizer/05-viewer.html\" rel=\"nofollow\">\n          <strong>Cube</strong>\n        </a>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <a href=\"https://vangelov.github.io/ts-rasterizer/03-texture.html\" rel=\"nofollow\">\n          <img src=\"/vangelov/ts-rasterizer/raw/main/screenshots/03-texture.png\" width=\"250\" alt=\"Texture\">\n        </a>\n      </td>\n      <td>\n        <a href=\"https://vangelov.github.io/ts-rasterizer/04-framebuffer.html\" rel=\"nofollow\">\n          <img src=\"/vangelov/ts-rasterizer/raw/main/screenshots/04-framebuffer.png\" width=\"250\" alt=\"Framebuffer\">\n        </a>\n      </td>\n      <td>\n        <a href=\"https://vangelov.github.io/ts-rasterizer/05-viewer.html\" rel=\"nofollow\">\n          <img src=\"/vangelov/ts-rasterizer/raw/main/screenshots/05-viewer.png\" width=\"250\" alt=\"Cube\">\n        </a>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <a href=\"https://vangelov.github.io/ts-rasterizer/06-model.html\" rel=\"nofollow\">\n          <strong>Model</strong>\n        </a>\n      </td>\n      <td>\n        <a href=\"https://vangelov.github.io/ts-rasterizer/07-blinn-phong.html\" rel=\"nofollow\">\n          <strong>Blinn-Phong</strong>\n        </a>\n      </td>\n      <td>\n        <a href=\"https://vangelov.github.io/ts-rasterizer/08-normal-mapping.html\" rel=\"nofollow\">\n          <strong>Normal Mapping</strong>\n        </a>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <a href=\"https://vangelov.github.io/ts-rasterizer/06-model.html\" rel=\"nofollow\">\n          <img src=\"/vangelov/ts-rasterizer/raw/main/screenshots/06-model.png\" width=\"250\" alt=\"Model\">\n        </a>\n         <br>\n          <a href=\"https://skfb.ly/on9Dn\" rel=\"nofollow\">\n            Sad toaster\n          </a>\n          by\n          <a href=\"https://sketchfab.com/tasha.lime\" rel=\"nofollow\">\n            Tasha.Lime\n          </a>\n      </td>\n      <td>\n        <a href=\"https://vangelov.github.io/ts-rasterizer/07-blinn-phong.html\" rel=\"nofollow\">\n          <img src=\"/vangelov/ts-rasterizer/raw/main/screenshots/07-blinn-phong.png\" width=\"250\" alt=\"Blinn-Phong\">\n        </a>\n      </td>\n      <td>\n        <a href=\"https://vangelov.github.io/ts-rasterizer/08-normal-mapping.html\" rel=\"nofollow\">\n          <img src=\"/vangelov/ts-rasterizer/raw/main/screenshots/08-normal-mapping.png\" width=\"250\" alt=\"Normal Mapping\">\n        </a>\n         <br>\n          <a href=\"https://sketchfab.com/3d-models/gameboy-cartridge-7c0160c8097a43e0a5e146bf4d7e01a1\" rel=\"nofollow\">\n            Gameboy Cartridge\n          </a>\n          by\n          <a href=\"https://sketchfab.com/KarolinaArts\" rel=\"nofollow\">\n            Karolina D\n          </a>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <a href=\"https://vangelov.github.io/ts-rasterizer/09-shadow-mapping.html\" rel=\"nofollow\">\n          <strong>Shadow Mapping</strong>\n        </a>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <a href=\"https://vangelov.github.io/ts-rasterizer/09-shadow-mapping.html\" rel=\"nofollow\">\n          <img src=\"/vangelov/ts-rasterizer/raw/main/screenshots/09-shadow-mapping.png\" width=\"250\" alt=\"Shadow Mapping\">\n        </a>\n        <br>\n        <a href=\"https://sketchfab.com/3d-models/low-poly-house-02635c7c191848699e88085c2ab27538\" rel=\"nofollow\">\n          low poly house\n        </a>\n        by\n        <a href=\"https://sketchfab.com/cofitelle\" rel=\"nofollow\">\n          cofitelle\n        </a>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </tbody></table></markdown-accessiblity-table>\n</div>\n<P dir=\"auto\"><h2 tabindex=\"-1\" dir=\"auto\">Example Code</h2><a id=\"user-content-example-code\" aria-label=\"Permalink: Example Code\" href=\"#example-code\"></a></P>\n<div dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"// Vertex attributes are stored in a single interleaved array.\n// Each vertex contains a position followed by a color.\n// prettier-ignore\nconst vertices = new Float32Array([\n  vec3(-1.0, 0.0, -1.0), vec3(1.0, 0.0, 0.0),\n  vec3(-1.0, 0.0,  1.0), vec3(1.0, 1.0, 1.0),\n  vec3( 1.0, 0.0,  1.0), vec3(0.0, 0.0, 1.0),\n  vec3( 1.0, 0.0, -1.0), vec3(0.0, 1.0, 0.0),\n]);\n\nconst indices = new Int32Array([0, 1, 2, 2, 3, 0]);\n\nconst renderer = new Renderer(document.getElementById(&quot;canvas&quot;) as HTMLCanvasElement, {\n  viewport: viewport(0, 0, 1280, 720),\n});\n\nconst program = new Program(\n  {\n    proj: mat4Perspective(radians(45.0), renderer.canvas.width / renderer.canvas.height, 1.0, 7.0),\n    view: mat4Mult(mat4Translation(vec3(-0.0, -0.25, -3.5)), mat4RotationX(radians(10))),\n  },\n\n  {\n    // Describes the attributes stored in each interleaved vertex.\n    vertexInput: [vec3, vec3],\n\n    // Describes the values produced by the vertex shader.\n    // The first output is the clip-space position.\n    vertexOutput: [vec4, vec3],\n  },\n\n  // Parameter types are inferred from the uniforms and shader layout.\n  (uniforms, vertexInput, vertexOutput) => {\n    const position = vertexInput[0];\n    const color = vertexInput[1];\n\n    vertexOutput[0] = mat4Multv(mat4Mult(uniforms.proj, uniforms.view), vec4From3(position, 1.0));\n\n    vertexOutput[1] = color;\n  },\n\n  // fragInput contains the interpolated vertex shader outputs.\n  // fragOutput[N] writes a color to render target N.\n  (_uniforms, fragInput, fragOutput) => {\n    const color = fragInput[1];\n    fragOutput[0] = vec4From3(color, 1.0);\n  },\n);\n\nconst clearColor = vec4(0, 0, 0, 1);\nrenderer.defaultFramebuffer.clearColorTargets(clearColor);\n\nrenderer.drawIndexed(vertices, indices, program);\"><pre><span>// Vertex attributes are stored in a single interleaved array.</span>\n<span>// Each vertex contains a position followed by a color.</span>\n<span>// prettier-ignore</span>\n<span>const</span> <span>vertices</span> <span>=</span> <span>new</span> <span>Float32Array</span><span>(</span><span>[</span>\n  <span>vec3</span><span>(</span><span>-</span><span>1.0</span><span>,</span> <span>0.0</span><span>,</span> <span>-</span><span>1.0</span><span>)</span><span>,</span> <span>vec3</span><span>(</span><span>1.0</span><span>,</span> <span>0.0</span><span>,</span> <span>0.0</span><span>)</span><span>,</span>\n  <span>vec3</span><span>(</span><span>-</span><span>1.0</span><span>,</span> <span>0.0</span><span>,</span>  <span>1.0</span><span>)</span><span>,</span> <span>vec3</span><span>(</span><span>1.0</span><span>,</span> <span>1.0</span><span>,</span> <span>1.0</span><span>)</span><span>,</span>\n  <span>vec3</span><span>(</span> <span>1.0</span><span>,</span> <span>0.0</span><span>,</span>  <span>1.0</span><span>)</span><span>,</span> <span>vec3</span><span>(</span><span>0.0</span><span>,</span> <span>0.0</span><span>,</span> <span>1.0</span><span>)</span><span>,</span>\n  <span>vec3</span><span>(</span> <span>1.0</span><span>,</span> <span>0.0</span><span>,</span> <span>-</span><span>1.0</span><span>)</span><span>,</span> <span>vec3</span><span>(</span><span>0.0</span><span>,</span> <span>1.0</span><span>,</span> <span>0.0</span><span>)</span><span>,</span>\n<span>]</span><span>)</span><span>;</span>\n\n<span>const</span> <span>indices</span> <span>=</span> <span>new</span> <span>Int32Array</span><span>(</span><span>[</span><span>0</span><span>,</span> <span>1</span><span>,</span> <span>2</span><span>,</span> <span>2</span><span>,</span> <span>3</span><span>,</span> <span>0</span><span>]</span><span>)</span><span>;</span>\n\n<span>const</span> <span>renderer</span> <span>=</span> <span>new</span> <span>Renderer</span><span>(</span><span>document</span><span>.</span><span>getElementById</span><span>(</span><span>\"canvas\"</span><span>)</span> <span>as</span> <span>HTMLCanvasElement</span><span>,</span> <span>{</span>\n  <span>viewport</span>: <span>viewport</span><span>(</span><span>0</span><span>,</span> <span>0</span><span>,</span> <span>1280</span><span>,</span> <span>720</span><span>)</span><span>,</span>\n<span>}</span><span>)</span><span>;</span>\n\n<span>const</span> <span>program</span> <span>=</span> <span>new</span> <span>Program</span><span>(</span>\n  <span>{</span>\n    <span>proj</span>: <span>mat4Perspective</span><span>(</span><span>radians</span><span>(</span><span>45.0</span><span>)</span><span>,</span> <span>renderer</span><span>.</span><span>canvas</span><span>.</span><span>width</span> <span>/</span> <span>renderer</span><span>.</span><span>canvas</span><span>.</span><span>height</span><span>,</span> <span>1.0</span><span>,</span> <span>7.0</span><span>)</span><span>,</span>\n    <span>view</span>: <span>mat4Mult</span><span>(</span><span>mat4Translation</span><span>(</span><span>vec3</span><span>(</span><span>-</span><span>0.0</span><span>,</span> <span>-</span><span>0.25</span><span>,</span> <span>-</span><span>3.5</span><span>)</span><span>)</span><span>,</span> <span>mat4RotationX</span><span>(</span><span>radians</span><span>(</span><span>10</span><span>)</span><span>)</span><span>)</span><span>,</span>\n  <span>}</span><span>,</span>\n\n  <span>{</span>\n    <span>// Describes the attributes stored in each interleaved vertex.</span>\n    <span>vertexInput</span>: <span>[</span><span>vec3</span><span>,</span> <span>vec3</span><span>]</span><span>,</span>\n\n    <span>// Describes the values produced by the vertex shader.</span>\n    <span>// The first output is the clip-space position.</span>\n    <span>vertexOutput</span>: <span>[</span><span>vec4</span><span>,</span> <span>vec3</span><span>]</span><span>,</span>\n  <span>}</span><span>,</span>\n\n  <span>// Parameter types are inferred from the uniforms and shader layout.</span>\n  <span>(</span><span>uniforms</span><span>,</span> <span>vertexInput</span><span>,</span> <span>vertexOutput</span><span>)</span> <span>=&gt;</span> <span>{</span>\n    <span>const</span> <span>position</span> <span>=</span> <span>vertexInput</span><span>[</span><span>0</span><span>]</span><span>;</span>\n    <span>const</span> <span>color</span> <span>=</span> <span>vertexInput</span><span>[</span><span>1</span><span>]</span><span>;</span>\n\n    <span>vertexOutput</span><span>[</span><span>0</span><span>]</span> <span>=</span> <span>mat4Multv</span><span>(</span><span>mat4Mult</span><span>(</span><span>uniforms</span><span>.</span><span>proj</span><span>,</span> <span>uniforms</span><span>.</span><span>view</span><span>)</span><span>,</span> <span>vec4From3</span><span>(</span><span>position</span><span>,</span> <span>1.0</span><span>)</span><span>)</span><span>;</span>\n\n    <span>vertexOutput</span><span>[</span><span>1</span><span>]</span> <span>=</span> <span>color</span><span>;</span>\n  <span>}</span><span>,</span>\n\n  <span>// fragInput contains the interpolated vertex shader outputs.</span>\n  <span>// fragOutput[N] writes a color to render target N.</span>\n  <span>(</span><span>_uniforms</span><span>,</span> <span>fragInput</span><span>,</span> <span>fragOutput</span><span>)</span> <span>=&gt;</span> <span>{</span>\n    <span>const</span> <span>color</span> <span>=</span> <span>fragInput</span><span>[</span><span>1</span><span>]</span><span>;</span>\n    <span>fragOutput</span><span>[</span><span>0</span><span>]</span> <span>=</span> <span>vec4From3</span><span>(</span><span>color</span><span>,</span> <span>1.0</span><span>)</span><span>;</span>\n  <span>}</span><span>,</span>\n<span>)</span><span>;</span>\n\n<span>const</span> <span>clearColor</span> <span>=</span> <span>vec4</span><span>(</span><span>0</span><span>,</span> <span>0</span><span>,</span> <span>0</span><span>,</span> <span>1</span><span>)</span><span>;</span>\n<span>renderer</span><span>.</span><span>defaultFramebuffer</span><span>.</span><span>clearColorTargets</span><span>(</span><span>clearColor</span><span>)</span><span>;</span>\n\n<span>renderer</span><span>.</span><span>drawIndexed</span><span>(</span><span>vertices</span><span>,</span> <span>indices</span><span>,</span> <span>program</span><span>)</span><span>;</span></pre></div>\n<P dir=\"auto\"><h2 tabindex=\"-1\" dir=\"auto\">Performance</h2><a id=\"user-content-performance\" aria-label=\"Permalink: Performance\" href=\"#performance\"></a></P>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The code is written to make the graphics pipeline easy to understand and modify, so readability is often preferred over maximum performance. While some parts are optimized where it makes sense, the main goal is to demonstrate how a software rasterizer works rather than to compete with GPU rendering.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">To support this, the project includes a small custom matrix and vector library designed around expression-style operations. Rather than creating temporary objects for every intermediate calculation, operations can reuse existing storage, reducing allocations and minimizing garbage collection while keeping the code concise.</p>\n</article></div></DIV>","content_text":"Overview A TypeScript CPU software rasterizer with programmable vertex and fragment shaders. Vertex layouts are fully customizable, allowing shaders to define and interpolate arbitrary vertex attributes. Credits The renderer is heavily based on Nikolaus Rauch's excellent C++ software rasterizer. Everything else—including the vector and matrix library, texture handling, sampling, and browser integration—was implemented specifically for this project and designed around the constraints of TypeScript and the web. The demos are adapted from Nikolaus's original project. Demos Triangle Plane Depth Texture Framebuffer Cube Model Blinn-Phong Normal Mapping Sad toaster by Tasha.Lime Gameboy Cartridge by Karolina D Shadow Mapping low poly house by cofitelle Example Code // Vertex attributes are stored in a single interleaved array. // Each vertex contains a position followed by a color. // prettier-ignore const vertices = new Float32Array([ vec3(-1.0, 0.0, -1.0), vec3(1.0, 0.0, 0.0), vec3(-1.0, 0.0, 1.0), vec3(1.0, 1.0, 1.0), vec3( 1.0, 0.0, 1.0), vec3(0.0, 0.0, 1.0), vec3( 1.0, 0.0, -1.0), vec3(0.0, 1.0, 0.0), ]); const indices = new Int32Array([0, 1, 2, 2, 3, 0]); const renderer = new Renderer(document.getElementById(\"canvas\") as HTMLCanvasElement, { viewport: viewport(0, 0, 1280, 720), }); const program = new Program( { proj: mat4Perspective(radians(45.0), renderer.canvas.width / renderer.canvas.height, 1.0, 7.0), view: mat4Mult(mat4Translation(vec3(-0.0, -0.25, -3.5)), mat4RotationX(radians(10))), }, { // Describes the attributes stored in each interleaved vertex. vertexInput: [vec3, vec3], // Describes the values produced by the vertex shader. // The first output is the clip-space position. vertexOutput: [vec4, vec3], }, // Parameter types are inferred from the uniforms and shader layout. (uniforms, vertexInput, vertexOutput) => { const position = vertexInput[0]; const color = vertexInput[1]; vertexOutput[0] = mat4Multv(mat4Mult(uniforms.proj, uniforms.view), vec4From3(position, 1.0)); vertexOutput[1] = color; }, // fragInput contains the interpolated vertex shader outputs. // fragOutput[N] writes a color to render target N. (_uniforms, fragInput, fragOutput) => { const color = fragInput[1]; fragOutput[0] = vec4From3(color, 1.0); }, ); const clearColor = vec4(0, 0, 0, 1); renderer.defaultFramebuffer.clearColorTargets(clearColor); renderer.drawIndexed(vertices, indices, program); Performance The code is written to make the graphics pipeline easy to understand and modify, so readability is often preferred over maximum performance. While some parts are optimized where it makes sense, the main goal is to demonstrate how a software rasterizer works rather than to compete with GPU rendering. To support this, the project includes a small custom matrix and vector library designed around expression-style operations. Rather than creating temporary objects for every intermediate calculation, operations can reuse existing storage, reducing allocations and minimizing garbage collection while keeping the code concise.","fetched_at":"2026-07-26T14:34:20.948Z","ok":true,"blocks":[{"html_en":"<h2 dir=\"auto\" tabindex=\"-1\">Overview</h2>","sentences":[{"en":"Overview","zh":"概述"}]},{"html_en":"<p dir=\"auto\">A TypeScript CPU software rasterizer with programmable vertex and fragment shaders. Vertex layouts are fully customizable, allowing shaders to define and interpolate arbitrary vertex attributes.</p>","sentences":[{"en":"A TypeScript CPU software rasterizer with programmable vertex and fragment shaders.","zh":"具有可编程顶点和片段着色器的 TypeScript CPU 软件光栅器。"},{"en":"Vertex layouts are fully customizable, allowing shaders to define and interpolate arbitrary vertex attributes.","zh":"顶点布局是完全可定制的，允许着色器定义和插入任意顶点属性。"}]},{"html_en":"<h2 dir=\"auto\" tabindex=\"-1\">Credits</h2>","sentences":[{"en":"Credits","zh":"制作人员"}]},{"html_en":"<p dir=\"auto\">The renderer is heavily based on Nikolaus Rauch's excellent <a href=\"https://github.com/nikolausrauch/software-rasterizer\">C++ software rasterizer</a>. Everything else—including the vector and matrix library, texture handling, sampling, and browser integration—was implemented specifically for this project and designed around the constraints of TypeScript and the web. The demos are adapted from Nikolaus's original project.</p>","sentences":[{"en":"The renderer is heavily based on Nikolaus Rauch's excellent C++ software rasterizer.","zh":"该渲染器很大程度上基于 Nikolaus Rauch 出色的 C++ 软件光栅化器。"},{"en":"Everything else—including the vector and matrix library, texture handling, sampling, and browser integration—was implemented specifically for this project and designed around the constraints of TypeScript and the web.","zh":"其他所有内容（包括矢量和矩阵库、纹理处理、采样和浏览器集成）都是专门针对该项目实现的，并围绕 TypeScript 和 Web 的约束进行设计。"},{"en":"The demos are adapted from Nikolaus's original project.","zh":"这些演示改编自 Nikolaus 的原始项目。"}]},{"html_en":"<h2 dir=\"auto\" tabindex=\"-1\">Demos</h2>","sentences":[]},{"html_en":"<td>\n        <a href=\"https://vangelov.github.io/ts-rasterizer/00-triangle.html\" rel=\"nofollow\">\n          <strong>Triangle</strong>\n        </a>\n      </td>","sentences":[{"en":"Triangle","zh":"三角形"}]},{"html_en":"<td>\n        <a href=\"https://vangelov.github.io/ts-rasterizer/01-plane.html\" rel=\"nofollow\">\n          <strong>Plane</strong>\n        </a>\n      </td>","sentences":[]},{"html_en":"<td>\n        <a href=\"https://vangelov.github.io/ts-rasterizer/02-depth-buffer.html\" rel=\"nofollow\">\n          <strong>Depth</strong>\n        </a>\n      </td>","sentences":[]},{"html_en":"<td>\n        <a href=\"https://vangelov.github.io/ts-rasterizer/03-texture.html\" rel=\"nofollow\">\n          <strong>Texture</strong>\n        </a>\n      </td>","sentences":[{"en":"Texture","zh":"质地"}]},{"html_en":"<td>\n        <a href=\"https://vangelov.github.io/ts-rasterizer/04-framebuffer.html\" rel=\"nofollow\">\n          <strong>Framebuffer</strong>\n        </a>\n      </td>","sentences":[{"en":"Framebuffer","zh":"帧缓冲"}]},{"html_en":"<td>\n        <a href=\"https://vangelov.github.io/ts-rasterizer/05-viewer.html\" rel=\"nofollow\">\n          <strong>Cube</strong>\n        </a>\n      </td>","sentences":[]},{"html_en":"<td>\n        <a href=\"https://vangelov.github.io/ts-rasterizer/06-model.html\" rel=\"nofollow\">\n          <strong>Model</strong>\n        </a>\n      </td>","sentences":[]},{"html_en":"<td>\n        <a href=\"https://vangelov.github.io/ts-rasterizer/07-blinn-phong.html\" rel=\"nofollow\">\n          <strong>Blinn-Phong</strong>\n        </a>\n      </td>","sentences":[{"en":"Blinn-Phong","zh":"布林-冯"}]},{"html_en":"<td>\n        <a href=\"https://vangelov.github.io/ts-rasterizer/08-normal-mapping.html\" rel=\"nofollow\">\n          <strong>Normal Mapping</strong>\n        </a>\n      </td>","sentences":[{"en":"Normal Mapping","zh":"法线贴图"}]},{"html_en":"<td>\n        <a href=\"https://vangelov.github.io/ts-rasterizer/06-model.html\" rel=\"nofollow\">\n          <img src=\"/vangelov/ts-rasterizer/raw/main/screenshots/06-model.png\" width=\"250\" alt=\"Model\">\n        </a>\n         <br>\n          <a href=\"https://skfb.ly/on9Dn\" rel=\"nofollow\">\n            Sad toaster\n          </a>\n          by\n          <a href=\"https://sketchfab.com/tasha.lime\" rel=\"nofollow\">\n            Tasha.Lime\n          </a>\n      </td>","sentences":[{"en":"Sad toaster by Tasha.Lime","zh":"悲伤的烤面包机作者：Tasha.Lime"}]},{"html_en":"<td>\n        <a href=\"https://vangelov.github.io/ts-rasterizer/08-normal-mapping.html\" rel=\"nofollow\">\n          <img src=\"/vangelov/ts-rasterizer/raw/main/screenshots/08-normal-mapping.png\" width=\"250\" alt=\"Normal Mapping\">\n        </a>\n         <br>\n          <a href=\"https://sketchfab.com/3d-models/gameboy-cartridge-7c0160c8097a43e0a5e146bf4d7e01a1\" rel=\"nofollow\">\n            Gameboy Cartridge\n          </a>\n          by\n          <a href=\"https://sketchfab.com/KarolinaArts\" rel=\"nofollow\">\n            Karolina D\n          </a>\n      </td>","sentences":[{"en":"Gameboy Cartridge by Karolina D","zh":"卡罗琳娜 D 设计的 Gameboy 墨盒"}]},{"html_en":"<td>\n        <a href=\"https://vangelov.github.io/ts-rasterizer/09-shadow-mapping.html\" rel=\"nofollow\">\n          <strong>Shadow Mapping</strong>\n        </a>\n      </td>","sentences":[{"en":"Shadow Mapping","zh":"阴影贴图"}]},{"html_en":"<td>\n        <a href=\"https://vangelov.github.io/ts-rasterizer/09-shadow-mapping.html\" rel=\"nofollow\">\n          <img src=\"/vangelov/ts-rasterizer/raw/main/screenshots/09-shadow-mapping.png\" width=\"250\" alt=\"Shadow Mapping\">\n        </a>\n        <br>\n        <a href=\"https://sketchfab.com/3d-models/low-poly-house-02635c7c191848699e88085c2ab27538\" rel=\"nofollow\">\n          low poly house\n        </a>\n        by\n        <a href=\"https://sketchfab.com/cofitelle\" rel=\"nofollow\">\n          cofitelle\n        </a>\n      </td>","sentences":[{"en":"low poly house by cofitelle","zh":"cofitelle 的低聚住宅"}]},{"html_en":"<h2 tabindex=\"-1\" dir=\"auto\">Example Code</h2>","sentences":[{"en":"Example Code","zh":"示例代码"}]},{"html_en":"<h2 tabindex=\"-1\" dir=\"auto\">Performance</h2>","sentences":[{"en":"Performance","zh":"表现"}]},{"html_en":"<p dir=\"auto\">The code is written to make the graphics pipeline easy to understand and modify, so readability is often preferred over maximum performance. While some parts are optimized where it makes sense, the main goal is to demonstrate how a software rasterizer works rather than to compete with GPU rendering.</p>","sentences":[{"en":"The code is written to make the graphics pipeline easy to understand and modify, so readability is often preferred over maximum performance.","zh":"编写代码是为了使图形管道易于理解和修改，因此可读性通常比最大性能更重要。"},{"en":"While some parts are optimized where it makes sense, the main goal is to demonstrate how a software rasterizer works rather than to compete with GPU rendering.","zh":"虽然某些部分在有意义的地方进行了优化，但主要目标是演示软件光栅化器的工作原理，而不是与 GPU 渲染竞争。"}]},{"html_en":"<p dir=\"auto\">To support this, the project includes a small custom matrix and vector library designed around expression-style operations. Rather than creating temporary objects for every intermediate calculation, operations can reuse existing storage, reducing allocations and minimizing garbage collection while keeping the code concise.</p>","sentences":[{"en":"To support this, the project includes a small custom matrix and vector library designed around expression-style operations.","zh":"为了支持这一点，该项目包括一个围绕表达式式操作设计的小型自定义矩阵和向量库。"},{"en":"Rather than creating temporary objects for every intermediate calculation, operations can reuse existing storage, reducing allocations and minimizing garbage collection while keeping the code concise.","zh":"操作可以重用现有存储，减少分配并最小化垃圾收集，同时保持代码简洁，而不是为每个中间计算创建临时对象。"}]}],"translated":true,"content_html_zh":"<div class=\"page\" id=\"readability-page-1\"><div data-hpc=\"true\" containertiming=\"hpc\"><article itemprop=\"text\"><p dir=\"auto\"></p><h2 dir=\"auto\" tabindex=\"-1\">概述</h2><a id=\"user-content-overview\" aria-label=\"Permalink: Overview\" href=\"#overview\"></a><p></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">具有可编程顶点和片段着色器的 TypeScript CPU 软件光栅器。 顶点布局是完全可定制的，允许着色器定义和插入任意顶点属性。</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"></p><h2 dir=\"auto\" tabindex=\"-1\">制作人员</h2><a id=\"user-content-credits\" aria-label=\"Permalink: Credits\" href=\"#credits\"></a><p></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">该渲染器很大程度上基于 Nikolaus Rauch 出色的 C++ 软件光栅化器。 其他所有内容（包括矢量和矩阵库、纹理处理、采样和浏览器集成）都是专门针对该项目实现的，并围绕 TypeScript 和 Web 的约束进行设计。 这些演示改编自 Nikolaus 的原始项目。</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"></p><h2 dir=\"auto\" tabindex=\"-1\">Demos</h2><a id=\"user-content-demos\" aria-label=\"Permalink: Demos\" href=\"#demos\"></a><p></p>\n<div dir=\"auto\">\n  <markdown-accessiblity-table><table>\n    <tbody><tr>\n      <td>三角形</td>\n      <td>\n        <a href=\"https://vangelov.github.io/ts-rasterizer/01-plane.html\" rel=\"nofollow\">\n          <strong>Plane</strong>\n        </a>\n      </td>\n      <td>\n        <a href=\"https://vangelov.github.io/ts-rasterizer/02-depth-buffer.html\" rel=\"nofollow\">\n          <strong>Depth</strong>\n        </a>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <a href=\"https://vangelov.github.io/ts-rasterizer/00-triangle.html\" rel=\"nofollow\">\n          <img src=\"/vangelov/ts-rasterizer/raw/main/screenshots/00-triangle.png\" width=\"250\" alt=\"Triangle\">\n        </a>\n      </td>\n      <td>\n        <a href=\"https://vangelov.github.io/ts-rasterizer/01-indexed-plane.html\" rel=\"nofollow\">\n          <img src=\"/vangelov/ts-rasterizer/raw/main/screenshots/01-indexed-plane.png\" width=\"250\" alt=\"Plane\">\n        </a>\n      </td>\n      <td>\n        <a href=\"https://vangelov.github.io/ts-rasterizer/02-depth-buffer.html\" rel=\"nofollow\">\n          <img src=\"/vangelov/ts-rasterizer/raw/main/screenshots/02-depth-buffer.png\" width=\"250\" alt=\"Depth\">\n        </a>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>质地</td>\n      <td>帧缓冲</td>\n      <td>\n        <a href=\"https://vangelov.github.io/ts-rasterizer/05-viewer.html\" rel=\"nofollow\">\n          <strong>Cube</strong>\n        </a>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <a href=\"https://vangelov.github.io/ts-rasterizer/03-texture.html\" rel=\"nofollow\">\n          <img src=\"/vangelov/ts-rasterizer/raw/main/screenshots/03-texture.png\" width=\"250\" alt=\"Texture\">\n        </a>\n      </td>\n      <td>\n        <a href=\"https://vangelov.github.io/ts-rasterizer/04-framebuffer.html\" rel=\"nofollow\">\n          <img src=\"/vangelov/ts-rasterizer/raw/main/screenshots/04-framebuffer.png\" width=\"250\" alt=\"Framebuffer\">\n        </a>\n      </td>\n      <td>\n        <a href=\"https://vangelov.github.io/ts-rasterizer/05-viewer.html\" rel=\"nofollow\">\n          <img src=\"/vangelov/ts-rasterizer/raw/main/screenshots/05-viewer.png\" width=\"250\" alt=\"Cube\">\n        </a>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <a href=\"https://vangelov.github.io/ts-rasterizer/06-model.html\" rel=\"nofollow\">\n          <strong>Model</strong>\n        </a>\n      </td>\n      <td>布林-冯</td>\n      <td>法线贴图</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>悲伤的烤面包机作者：Tasha.Lime</td>\n      <td>\n        <a href=\"https://vangelov.github.io/ts-rasterizer/07-blinn-phong.html\" rel=\"nofollow\">\n          <img src=\"/vangelov/ts-rasterizer/raw/main/screenshots/07-blinn-phong.png\" width=\"250\" alt=\"Blinn-Phong\">\n        </a>\n      </td>\n      <td>卡罗琳娜 D 设计的 Gameboy 墨盒</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>阴影贴图</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>cofitelle 的低聚住宅</td>\n    </tr>\n  </tbody></table></markdown-accessiblity-table>\n</div>\n<p dir=\"auto\"></p><h2 tabindex=\"-1\" dir=\"auto\">示例代码</h2><a id=\"user-content-example-code\" aria-label=\"Permalink: Example Code\" href=\"#example-code\"></a><p></p>\n<div dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"// Vertex attributes are stored in a single interleaved array.\n// Each vertex contains a position followed by a color.\n// prettier-ignore\nconst vertices = new Float32Array([\n  vec3(-1.0, 0.0, -1.0), vec3(1.0, 0.0, 0.0),\n  vec3(-1.0, 0.0,  1.0), vec3(1.0, 1.0, 1.0),\n  vec3( 1.0, 0.0,  1.0), vec3(0.0, 0.0, 1.0),\n  vec3( 1.0, 0.0, -1.0), vec3(0.0, 1.0, 0.0),\n]);\n\nconst indices = new Int32Array([0, 1, 2, 2, 3, 0]);\n\nconst renderer = new Renderer(document.getElementById(&quot;canvas&quot;) as HTMLCanvasElement, {\n  viewport: viewport(0, 0, 1280, 720),\n});\n\nconst program = new Program(\n  {\n    proj: mat4Perspective(radians(45.0), renderer.canvas.width / renderer.canvas.height, 1.0, 7.0),\n    view: mat4Mult(mat4Translation(vec3(-0.0, -0.25, -3.5)), mat4RotationX(radians(10))),\n  },\n\n  {\n    // Describes the attributes stored in each interleaved vertex.\n    vertexInput: [vec3, vec3],\n\n    // Describes the values produced by the vertex shader.\n    // The first output is the clip-space position.\n    vertexOutput: [vec4, vec3],\n  },\n\n  // Parameter types are inferred from the uniforms and shader layout.\n  (uniforms, vertexInput, vertexOutput) => {\n    const position = vertexInput[0];\n    const color = vertexInput[1];\n\n    vertexOutput[0] = mat4Multv(mat4Mult(uniforms.proj, uniforms.view), vec4From3(position, 1.0));\n\n    vertexOutput[1] = color;\n  },\n\n  // fragInput contains the interpolated vertex shader outputs.\n  // fragOutput[N] writes a color to render target N.\n  (_uniforms, fragInput, fragOutput) => {\n    const color = fragInput[1];\n    fragOutput[0] = vec4From3(color, 1.0);\n  },\n);\n\nconst clearColor = vec4(0, 0, 0, 1);\nrenderer.defaultFramebuffer.clearColorTargets(clearColor);\n\nrenderer.drawIndexed(vertices, indices, program);\"><pre><span>// Vertex attributes are stored in a single interleaved array.</span>\n<span>// Each vertex contains a position followed by a color.</span>\n<span>// prettier-ignore</span>\n<span>const</span> <span>vertices</span> <span>=</span> <span>new</span> <span>Float32Array</span><span>(</span><span>[</span>\n  <span>vec3</span><span>(</span><span>-</span><span>1.0</span><span>,</span> <span>0.0</span><span>,</span> <span>-</span><span>1.0</span><span>)</span><span>,</span> <span>vec3</span><span>(</span><span>1.0</span><span>,</span> <span>0.0</span><span>,</span> <span>0.0</span><span>)</span><span>,</span>\n  <span>vec3</span><span>(</span><span>-</span><span>1.0</span><span>,</span> <span>0.0</span><span>,</span>  <span>1.0</span><span>)</span><span>,</span> <span>vec3</span><span>(</span><span>1.0</span><span>,</span> <span>1.0</span><span>,</span> <span>1.0</span><span>)</span><span>,</span>\n  <span>vec3</span><span>(</span> <span>1.0</span><span>,</span> <span>0.0</span><span>,</span>  <span>1.0</span><span>)</span><span>,</span> <span>vec3</span><span>(</span><span>0.0</span><span>,</span> <span>0.0</span><span>,</span> <span>1.0</span><span>)</span><span>,</span>\n  <span>vec3</span><span>(</span> <span>1.0</span><span>,</span> <span>0.0</span><span>,</span> <span>-</span><span>1.0</span><span>)</span><span>,</span> <span>vec3</span><span>(</span><span>0.0</span><span>,</span> <span>1.0</span><span>,</span> <span>0.0</span><span>)</span><span>,</span>\n<span>]</span><span>)</span><span>;</span>\n\n<span>const</span> <span>indices</span> <span>=</span> <span>new</span> <span>Int32Array</span><span>(</span><span>[</span><span>0</span><span>,</span> <span>1</span><span>,</span> <span>2</span><span>,</span> <span>2</span><span>,</span> <span>3</span><span>,</span> <span>0</span><span>]</span><span>)</span><span>;</span>\n\n<span>const</span> <span>renderer</span> <span>=</span> <span>new</span> <span>Renderer</span><span>(</span><span>document</span><span>.</span><span>getElementById</span><span>(</span><span>\"canvas\"</span><span>)</span> <span>as</span> <span>HTMLCanvasElement</span><span>,</span> <span>{</span>\n  <span>viewport</span>: <span>viewport</span><span>(</span><span>0</span><span>,</span> <span>0</span><span>,</span> <span>1280</span><span>,</span> <span>720</span><span>)</span><span>,</span>\n<span>}</span><span>)</span><span>;</span>\n\n<span>const</span> <span>program</span> <span>=</span> <span>new</span> <span>Program</span><span>(</span>\n  <span>{</span>\n    <span>proj</span>: <span>mat4Perspective</span><span>(</span><span>radians</span><span>(</span><span>45.0</span><span>)</span><span>,</span> <span>renderer</span><span>.</span><span>canvas</span><span>.</span><span>width</span> <span>/</span> <span>renderer</span><span>.</span><span>canvas</span><span>.</span><span>height</span><span>,</span> <span>1.0</span><span>,</span> <span>7.0</span><span>)</span><span>,</span>\n    <span>view</span>: <span>mat4Mult</span><span>(</span><span>mat4Translation</span><span>(</span><span>vec3</span><span>(</span><span>-</span><span>0.0</span><span>,</span> <span>-</span><span>0.25</span><span>,</span> <span>-</span><span>3.5</span><span>)</span><span>)</span><span>,</span> <span>mat4RotationX</span><span>(</span><span>radians</span><span>(</span><span>10</span><span>)</span><span>)</span><span>)</span><span>,</span>\n  <span>}</span><span>,</span>\n\n  <span>{</span>\n    <span>// Describes the attributes stored in each interleaved vertex.</span>\n    <span>vertexInput</span>: <span>[</span><span>vec3</span><span>,</span> <span>vec3</span><span>]</span><span>,</span>\n\n    <span>// Describes the values produced by the vertex shader.</span>\n    <span>// The first output is the clip-space position.</span>\n    <span>vertexOutput</span>: <span>[</span><span>vec4</span><span>,</span> <span>vec3</span><span>]</span><span>,</span>\n  <span>}</span><span>,</span>\n\n  <span>// Parameter types are inferred from the uniforms and shader layout.</span>\n  <span>(</span><span>uniforms</span><span>,</span> <span>vertexInput</span><span>,</span> <span>vertexOutput</span><span>)</span> <span>=&gt;</span> <span>{</span>\n    <span>const</span> <span>position</span> <span>=</span> <span>vertexInput</span><span>[</span><span>0</span><span>]</span><span>;</span>\n    <span>const</span> <span>color</span> <span>=</span> <span>vertexInput</span><span>[</span><span>1</span><span>]</span><span>;</span>\n\n    <span>vertexOutput</span><span>[</span><span>0</span><span>]</span> <span>=</span> <span>mat4Multv</span><span>(</span><span>mat4Mult</span><span>(</span><span>uniforms</span><span>.</span><span>proj</span><span>,</span> <span>uniforms</span><span>.</span><span>view</span><span>)</span><span>,</span> <span>vec4From3</span><span>(</span><span>position</span><span>,</span> <span>1.0</span><span>)</span><span>)</span><span>;</span>\n\n    <span>vertexOutput</span><span>[</span><span>1</span><span>]</span> <span>=</span> <span>color</span><span>;</span>\n  <span>}</span><span>,</span>\n\n  <span>// fragInput contains the interpolated vertex shader outputs.</span>\n  <span>// fragOutput[N] writes a color to render target N.</span>\n  <span>(</span><span>_uniforms</span><span>,</span> <span>fragInput</span><span>,</span> <span>fragOutput</span><span>)</span> <span>=&gt;</span> <span>{</span>\n    <span>const</span> <span>color</span> <span>=</span> <span>fragInput</span><span>[</span><span>1</span><span>]</span><span>;</span>\n    <span>fragOutput</span><span>[</span><span>0</span><span>]</span> <span>=</span> <span>vec4From3</span><span>(</span><span>color</span><span>,</span> <span>1.0</span><span>)</span><span>;</span>\n  <span>}</span><span>,</span>\n<span>)</span><span>;</span>\n\n<span>const</span> <span>clearColor</span> <span>=</span> <span>vec4</span><span>(</span><span>0</span><span>,</span> <span>0</span><span>,</span> <span>0</span><span>,</span> <span>1</span><span>)</span><span>;</span>\n<span>renderer</span><span>.</span><span>defaultFramebuffer</span><span>.</span><span>clearColorTargets</span><span>(</span><span>clearColor</span><span>)</span><span>;</span>\n\n<span>renderer</span><span>.</span><span>drawIndexed</span><span>(</span><span>vertices</span><span>,</span> <span>indices</span><span>,</span> <span>program</span><span>)</span><span>;</span></pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\"></p><h2 tabindex=\"-1\" dir=\"auto\">表现</h2><a id=\"user-content-performance\" aria-label=\"Permalink: Performance\" href=\"#performance\"></a><p></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">编写代码是为了使图形管道易于理解和修改，因此可读性通常比最大性能更重要。 虽然某些部分在有意义的地方进行了优化，但主要目标是演示软件光栅化器的工作原理，而不是与 GPU 渲染竞争。</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">为了支持这一点，该项目包括一个围绕表达式式操作设计的小型自定义矩阵和向量库。 操作可以重用现有存储，减少分配并最小化垃圾收集，同时保持代码简洁，而不是为每个中间计算创建临时对象。</p>\n</article></div></div>"}